Quote the alias of the events index stats

Why: EventIndexStatsBehavior::aggregate() names the alias Event unquoted. PostgreSQL folds it to event while the FROM clause quotes it as "Event", so the events index answers 500 for a user on the Overmind theme, MISP 3.0's default.
Upstream: not filed yet

diff --git a/app/Model/Behavior/EventIndexStatsBehavior.php b/app/Model/Behavior/EventIndexStatsBehavior.php
--- a/app/Model/Behavior/EventIndexStatsBehavior.php
+++ b/app/Model/Behavior/EventIndexStatsBehavior.php
@@ -47,9 +47,10 @@ class EventIndexStatsBehavior extends ModelBehavior
      */
     public function aggregate(Model $model, $conditions)
     {
-        $alias = $model->alias;
+        // PostgreSQL folds an unquoted alias to lower case, and the FROM clause quotes it
+        $alias = $model->getDataSource()->name($model->alias);
         $weekAgo = time() - self::WEEK;
-        $lastLogin = (int)$this->settings[$alias]['lastLogin'];
+        $lastLogin = (int)$this->settings[$model->alias]['lastLogin'];
         $sum = function ($condition) {
             return 'SUM(CASE WHEN ' . $condition . ' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)';
         };
